CORE broken-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--smt2 --outfile -
^\(set-logic AUFBV\)$
^\(assert \(forall
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
QF_AUFBV
--
The generic SMT2 encoding writes a zero-initialised array of symbolic size
(array_of without `as const') as a universally quantified assertion.  A
logic named QF_... admits no quantifiers, so the declared logic is AUFBV;
z3 and cvc5 rejected the file ("logic does not support quantifiers").
broken-smt-backend: the test inspects the generic output only.
